WEBVTT

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.067
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.272
Voyager, do you read?

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.043
You must lie still.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.607
I-I-I can't feel my legs.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.349
Several of your vertebrae
have been fractured.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.950
Isn't there anything you can do?

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:29.052
I'm afraid the shuttle's
medical supplies are inadequate.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.290
We must wait
for Voyager to find us.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.155
It's getting worse.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.667
My whole body feels numb.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.397
I want you to slow
your breathing

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:39.428
and relax your muscles.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.337
Try not to move.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.968
A-All this time I thought...

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.773
I thought I was so lucky...

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.144
no family back home...

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.513
nobody to miss.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.850
Now it seems kind of sad not,
not to leave anybody behind.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.221
I believe Ensign Macormak
would miss you a great deal.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.960
You think so?

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:05.624
I was never really sure
how sh... sh...

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.493
It's all right.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.359
Don't be frightened.
I won't hurt you.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.728
Let me go!

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.062
Will you run if I do?

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.162
No.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:49.837
My name is Tuvok.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:50.843
Who are you?

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.845
Tressa.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.403
You don't look like us.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.506
I am not a member of your race.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.608
I am Vulcan.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.484
I thought this moon
was uninhabited.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:02.920
Do you live here?

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:06.087
We came here on a ship,

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.458
but it crashed, like yours.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.222
Where are your parents?

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.787
Dead.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.831
Is he dead, too?

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.836
Yes.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.360
What were you doing to him?

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.998
I put a stasis field
around his body to protect it

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.769
until I can take it back
to my ship.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:23.901
Why?

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.810
Some cultures,
like Mr. Bennet's,

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.474
consider an appropriate burial
to be a sign of respect.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.949
Tressa, is there anyone else
here with you?

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.118
It's all right.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.254
There is no one
looking after you?

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.767
Everyone else died
in the crash.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.530
We're alone.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.134
There is no reason to be afraid.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:00.578
I will take care of you now and
see that you get home safely.

00:05:00.698 --> 00:05:02.757
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.267
I've sent out scouting parties

00:05:04.301 --> 00:05:08.260
to analyze the mineral deposits
in the moons around Drayan II.

00:05:08.305 --> 00:05:10.569
Meanwhile,
I've arranged a meeting

00:05:10.608 --> 00:05:12.906
with the planet's leader.

00:05:12.943 --> 00:05:15.173
According to Neelix,
nobody's had direct contact

00:05:15.212 --> 00:05:16.577
with the Drayans for decades.

00:05:16.614 --> 00:05:17.911
All he's heard are rumors.

00:05:17.948 --> 00:05:19.973
Do any of those rumors
describe them as hostile?

00:05:20.017 --> 00:05:21.609
No. Just very private.

00:05:21.652 --> 00:05:22.949
That's something.

00:05:22.987 --> 00:05:24.648
Deck 4.

00:05:24.688 --> 00:05:26.417
My diplomacy professor
used to say

00:05:26.457 --> 00:05:29.051
the opening 20 minutes
of a first-contact situation

00:05:29.093 --> 00:05:30.651
are the most crucial.

00:05:30.694 --> 00:05:32.628
I'd feel better
about this particular 20 minutes

00:05:32.663 --> 00:05:34.358
if we had some idea
what to expect.

00:05:34.398 --> 00:05:36.389
Sometimes, you have
to go in blind.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:37.560
That's the exciting part.

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:39.296
When I was a Science Officer,

00:05:39.336 --> 00:05:41.600
I always envied
the Captain's privilege

00:05:41.639 --> 00:05:44.073
of making first contact
with new races.

00:05:44.108 --> 00:05:46.372
I envied it so much,

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.469
I almost got myself shipped
back to the Academy

00:05:48.579 --> 00:05:49.910
for remedial training.

00:05:49.947 --> 00:05:52.108
On my first assignment,

00:05:52.149 --> 00:05:54.743
we were sent to make contact
with the Tarkannans.

00:05:54.785 --> 00:05:56.946
I studied all the information
we had about them

00:05:56.987 --> 00:05:58.887
and pestered the Captain
into letting me be part

00:05:58.923 --> 00:06:00.185
of the diplomatic team.

00:06:00.224 --> 00:06:03.284
When we came face-to-face
with the Tarkannan delegation,

00:06:03.327 --> 00:06:06.194
I very proudly made the
traditional gesture for "hello,"

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.562
not realizing that males
and females of their race

00:06:08.599 --> 00:06:11.227
use different styles
of movement, and I was

00:06:11.268 --> 00:06:13.600
actually propositioning
the ambassador.

00:06:15.005 --> 00:06:16.336
Energize.

00:06:26.116 --> 00:06:28.141
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:06:28.185 --> 00:06:32.019
I'd like to welcome you aboard
the Federation Starship Voyager.

00:06:32.056 --> 00:06:34.320
First Prelate Alcia.

00:06:34.358 --> 00:06:36.349
May this day find you at peace

00:06:36.393 --> 00:06:37.985
and leave you with hope.

00:06:38.028 --> 00:06:39.120
That's a traditional
blessing

00:06:39.163 --> 00:06:40.926
from our ancient scrolls.

00:06:40.965 --> 00:06:42.865
Om-nah-hoo-pez-nyeetz.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.595
That's from the spirits
of my people.

00:06:44.635 --> 00:06:48.127
It means, "peace in your heart,
fortune in your steps."

00:06:48.172 --> 00:06:51.039
It's very gracious of you
to agree to meet with us.

00:06:51.075 --> 00:06:55.136
We don't often engage in
dialogue with alien races,

00:06:55.179 --> 00:06:58.171
but your story of crossing
the galaxy intrigued me.

00:06:58.215 --> 00:07:01.412
I'd be glad to tell you all
about our journey and my crew.

00:07:01.452 --> 00:07:04.649
Perhaps you'd like to see
more of our ship as well.

00:07:04.688 --> 00:07:06.280
Thank you.

00:07:18.302 --> 00:07:20.429
Our warp core
is designed to operate

00:07:20.504 --> 00:07:23.098
for up to three years
before refueling.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.973
The reaction chamber is
equipped with a compositor,

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.376
which allows us to recrystallize
the dilithium.

00:07:28.412 --> 00:07:30.346
In our situation,
we can never be sure

00:07:30.381 --> 00:07:32.349
when we'll be able
to find a new supply.

00:07:32.383 --> 00:07:35.147
I'm sorry my Chief Engineer
isn't here to meet you.

00:07:35.185 --> 00:07:36.846
She's leading one
of the away teams

00:07:36.887 --> 00:07:39.014
surveying the moons
around Drayan.

00:07:39.056 --> 00:07:40.614
I find it interesting

00:07:40.658 --> 00:07:43.422
that you chose this
to show me first.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.452
Do your people consider
advanced technology

00:07:46.497 --> 00:07:48.260
to be their highest achievement?

00:07:48.299 --> 00:07:49.789
Not as an end in itself.

00:07:49.833 --> 00:07:51.357
The purpose of all this

00:07:51.402 --> 00:07:54.166
is to help us gain knowledge
about the universe

00:07:54.204 --> 00:07:55.671
and the people in it.

00:07:55.706 --> 00:07:59.267
Our ancestors were brilliant
scientists and engineers.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.800
They were continually developing

00:08:00.844 --> 00:08:03.836
better, smarter,
more efficient machines,

00:08:03.881 --> 00:08:04.848
until the technology

00:08:04.882 --> 00:08:07.373
became more important
than the people.

00:08:07.418 --> 00:08:09.545
I believe that society
would have self-destructed

00:08:09.587 --> 00:08:11.521
if it weren't
for the Reformation.

00:08:11.555 --> 00:08:14.353
My great-grandfather
helped to return us

00:08:14.391 --> 00:08:16.723
to ourselves,
and since that time,

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.127
we've remained isolated
to avoid the influence

00:08:20.164 --> 00:08:22.792
of those who might lead us
back down the wrong path.

00:08:22.833 --> 00:08:26.064
Some human cultures
have done the same.

00:08:32.376 --> 00:08:34.276
Will your friend be
all right in there?

00:08:34.311 --> 00:08:37.610
Yes, I have secured his body
within the stasis field.

00:08:37.648 --> 00:08:40.412
You are all very fortunate
to have escaped the crash

00:08:40.451 --> 00:08:41.782
with only a few bruises.

00:08:41.819 --> 00:08:43.980
The attendants protected us.

00:08:44.021 --> 00:08:44.988
Attendants?

00:08:45.022 --> 00:08:46.011
The people on our ship...

00:08:46.056 --> 00:08:48.047
they got us to the escape pod

00:08:48.092 --> 00:08:49.457
before they crashed.

00:08:49.526 --> 00:08:50.618
Can we go now?

00:08:50.661 --> 00:08:52.026
I want to go.

00:08:52.062 --> 00:08:53.757
Are we going to fly
in your ship?

00:08:53.797 --> 00:08:56.630
He said it was a shuttle,
not a ship.

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:57.964
We cannot leave yet.

00:08:58.002 --> 00:08:59.799
My shuttle
is in need of repairs.

00:08:59.837 --> 00:09:01.327
Can't you fix it?

00:09:01.372 --> 00:09:02.396
I believe so.

00:09:02.439 --> 00:09:04.999
However, I am more concerned
with getting through

00:09:05.042 --> 00:09:07.067
the electrodynamic turbulence
in the ionosphere.

00:09:07.111 --> 00:09:09.375
What's electro turbulence?

00:09:09.413 --> 00:09:11.404
A thermal inversion gradient

00:09:11.448 --> 00:09:14.008
is causing unusually strong
and unpredictable currents

00:09:14.051 --> 00:09:15.916
in the upper levels
of the atmosphere.

00:09:15.953 --> 00:09:18.979
Those currents caused
my shuttle to crash,

00:09:19.023 --> 00:09:20.888
and I assume, yours as well.

00:09:20.924 --> 00:09:23.688
I must find a way to safely
navigate through the turbulence

00:09:23.727 --> 00:09:25.194
before we can attempt to leave.

00:09:25.229 --> 00:09:26.821
Will that take a long time?

00:09:26.864 --> 00:09:29.389
It may.
You must be patient.

00:09:29.433 --> 00:09:31.162
I don't want
to stay here anymore.

00:09:31.201 --> 00:09:33.328
I don't like it here.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.804
Your displeasure doesn't change
our situation,

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:38.103
nor does it bring us
any closer to a solution.

00:09:38.142 --> 00:09:40.076
You don't have to be
so mean about it.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:42.101
It isn't my intention
to be mean.

00:09:42.146 --> 00:09:44.944
I only wish to provide you
with a realistic assessment.

00:09:44.982 --> 00:09:48.611
Vulcan parents never shield
their children from the truth.

00:09:48.652 --> 00:09:50.813
Doing so would only hinder
their ability to cope

00:09:50.854 --> 00:09:52.446
with inevitable difficulties.

00:09:52.556 --> 00:09:54.387
I'm hungry.

00:09:54.425 --> 00:09:57.451
There is a supply of Starfleet
rations in the shuttle.

00:09:57.494 --> 00:09:59.086
What's rations?

00:09:59.129 --> 00:10:02.155
Concentrated, vitamin-enriched
nutritional supplements.

00:10:02.199 --> 00:10:04.064
I want takka berries.

00:10:04.101 --> 00:10:06.296
With cherel sauce.

00:10:06.336 --> 00:10:08.531
We have only rations.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:12.570
Now, I must begin working
on my shuttle.

00:10:12.609 --> 00:10:14.042
By my estimate, we have fewer

00:10:14.078 --> 00:10:15.670
than four hours
of daylight remaining.

00:10:15.713 --> 00:10:17.476
We can't be here
when it's night.

00:10:17.514 --> 00:10:19.277
That's when the morrok comes.

00:10:19.316 --> 00:10:21.147
Is that a species of animal?

00:10:21.185 --> 00:10:23.710
The morrok is what
takes you when you die.

00:10:23.754 --> 00:10:25.278
It lives here...

00:10:25.322 --> 00:10:26.914
in the cave.

00:10:33.363 --> 00:10:36.696
I'm not detecting any life-forms
other than ourselves.

00:10:36.734 --> 00:10:38.201
It's here.

00:10:38.235 --> 00:10:40.169
It'll come.

00:10:41.705 --> 00:10:43.605
Have any of you ever
seen this creature?

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.006
You can only see it
when it comes for you.

00:10:46.043 --> 00:10:47.635
Then it's too late.

00:10:47.678 --> 00:10:50.909
I believe your anxiety
about our situation

00:10:50.948 --> 00:10:52.415
is causing you
to imagine the presence...

00:10:52.449 --> 00:10:53.416
It took the others!

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.384
Jarren and Fayla...

00:10:55.419 --> 00:10:57.080
the other children on the ship.

00:10:57.121 --> 00:10:59.612
The morrok took them
while we were sleeping...

00:10:59.656 --> 00:11:02.284
and tonight, it will take us.

00:11:17.941 --> 00:11:21.104
The Federation consists
of over 150 different worlds

00:11:21.145 --> 00:11:23.705
who have agreed to share
their knowledge and resources

00:11:23.747 --> 00:11:26.181
in peaceful cooperation.

00:11:26.216 --> 00:11:28.207
Ah, visitors.

00:11:28.252 --> 00:11:29.651
Welcome to Sick Bay.

00:11:29.686 --> 00:11:31.278
I'm the Chief Medical Officer.

00:11:31.321 --> 00:11:34.620
This is First Prelate
Alcia of Drayan II.

00:11:34.658 --> 00:11:36.649
It's an honor to meet you.

00:11:36.693 --> 00:11:39.093
We don't often receive
such distinguished guests here,

00:11:39.129 --> 00:11:41.563
unless there's been
some sort of accident.

00:11:44.268 --> 00:11:46.759
I'm... sure nothing unfortunate
will happen to you

00:11:46.804 --> 00:11:49.500
on your visit here, but if
it did, you can rest assured

00:11:49.606 --> 00:11:51.870
you will find yourself
in very capable hands.

00:11:51.909 --> 00:11:53.809
We are fully equipped to provide

00:11:53.844 --> 00:11:55.675
a wide variety
of treatments here,

00:11:55.712 --> 00:11:57.703
from removing a splinter

00:11:57.748 --> 00:12:01.582
to resequencing the base pairs
in a strand of DNA.

00:12:01.618 --> 00:12:04.280
And our research facilities

00:12:04.321 --> 00:12:06.789
are the most advanced
in Starfleet.

00:12:06.824 --> 00:12:08.451
Very impressive.

00:12:08.559 --> 00:12:10.083
You may be even more
interested to learn

00:12:10.127 --> 00:12:12.823
that this man isn't really
a biological life-form.

00:12:12.863 --> 00:12:16.663
He's a computer-generated
holographic projection.

00:12:21.672 --> 00:12:23.367
My people believe

00:12:23.407 --> 00:12:26.103
that physical matter's
only an illusion.

00:12:26.143 --> 00:12:28.407
The body is not the true self,

00:12:28.445 --> 00:12:30.208
only a representation.

00:12:30.247 --> 00:12:32.477
One of our greatest
philosophers, Plato,

00:12:32.549 --> 00:12:34.380
wrote that what we see around us

00:12:34.418 --> 00:12:36.682
are only poor shadows
of ideal objects,

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.483
which exist on a higher plane.

00:12:38.555 --> 00:12:41.023
That is similar
to our teachings.

00:12:41.058 --> 00:12:44.152
Our connection to what you call
a higher plane

00:12:44.194 --> 00:12:46.685
is more important
than our attachment

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:49.221
to this brief existence,
however real it may seem.

00:12:49.266 --> 00:12:50.324
Bridge to Captain.

00:12:50.367 --> 00:12:52.733
There's an incoming message
for the First Prelate.

00:12:52.769 --> 00:12:54.896
Perhaps you'd like
to use my office.

00:12:54.938 --> 00:12:58.135
Uh, yes.
Thank you, Doctor?

00:12:58.175 --> 00:13:00.268
I'm afraid it's just Doctor.

00:13:02.513 --> 00:13:04.242
Patch it through
on a secure channel

00:13:04.281 --> 00:13:05.873
to the Doctor's office, Mr. Kim.

00:13:05.916 --> 00:13:07.406
Acknowledged.

00:13:07.451 --> 00:13:08.418
You did very well.

00:13:08.452 --> 00:13:09.578
I think she was impressed.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.111
Kes has been coaching me
on my diplomatic skills.

00:13:12.155 --> 00:13:14.123
It shows.

00:13:14.157 --> 00:13:16.421
Our next step will be
to open negotiations...

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:17.757
find out what they
might be interested

00:13:17.794 --> 00:13:18.954
in getting from us

00:13:18.996 --> 00:13:21.191
in exchange
for the polyferranide.

00:13:22.332 --> 00:13:24.459
I've been called away
on an emergency.

00:13:24.501 --> 00:13:26.901
Is there anything
we can do to help?

00:13:26.937 --> 00:13:28.029
No. Thank you.

00:13:28.071 --> 00:13:29.368
It would be better
if you and your crew

00:13:29.406 --> 00:13:30.373
continued on your journey.

00:13:30.407 --> 00:13:32.341
It's been an interesting visit.

00:13:32.376 --> 00:13:34.571
We'd been hoping
to learn more about you.

00:13:34.611 --> 00:13:37.808
It's been our custom
for generations

00:13:37.848 --> 00:13:40.180
to avoid close contact
with outsiders.

00:13:40.217 --> 00:13:42.845
I choose to honor
that tradition.

00:13:42.886 --> 00:13:44.649
Good-bye, Captain.

00:13:44.688 --> 00:13:46.849
I hope you find your way home.

00:13:51.295 --> 00:13:52.728
Was it something I said?

00:13:52.763 --> 00:13:54.458
We could assure her
we have no intention

00:13:54.498 --> 00:13:56.489
of interfering with their
culture or traditions.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.830
No. She made her wishes clear.

00:13:58.869 --> 00:14:00.837
If we're not welcome, we'll go.

00:14:00.871 --> 00:14:02.304
Recall the scouting parties.

00:14:02.339 --> 00:14:05.831
We'll have to find our
polyferranide somewhere else.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.135
Where did you last see
the missing children?

00:14:09.179 --> 00:14:12.444
By the big tree when we
went to sleep last night.

00:14:12.516 --> 00:14:13.813
Were either of them injured?

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.374
Jarren hurt his hand.

00:14:15.419 --> 00:14:16.886
But both were able to walk?

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:17.887
Uh-huh.

00:14:17.921 --> 00:14:19.980
Did any of you hear them
get up during the night?

00:14:20.023 --> 00:14:22.617
You think they wandered
off and got lost,

00:14:22.659 --> 00:14:23.648
but they didn't.

00:14:23.694 --> 00:14:25.286
The morrok took them.

00:14:25.329 --> 00:14:26.421
They're gone.

00:14:26.463 --> 00:14:27.452
The other children

00:14:27.497 --> 00:14:29.124
aren't within scanning range
of this tricorder.

00:14:29.166 --> 00:14:31.361
That is the only thing we know
for certain at this time.

00:14:31.401 --> 00:14:32.891
You don't understand.

00:14:32.936 --> 00:14:34.597
We have to get away from here.

00:14:34.638 --> 00:14:35.969
Please, can we go?

00:14:36.006 --> 00:14:37.337
I'm scared.

00:14:37.374 --> 00:14:38.466
Please, Tuvok?

00:14:38.508 --> 00:14:42.103
Children, you are allowing
your fears to guide you.

00:14:42.145 --> 00:14:44.204
You must learn
to exercise control

00:14:44.247 --> 00:14:45.236
over your own imagination.

00:14:45.282 --> 00:14:46.249
But the morrok!

00:14:46.283 --> 00:14:47.409
Yes.

00:14:47.451 --> 00:14:50.284
The existence of such a creature
is one possibility.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.016
However, your emotional
reactions are preventing you

00:14:53.056 --> 00:14:56.048
from accurately judging
how unlikely that is to be true.

00:14:56.093 --> 00:14:57.287
I can't help it.

00:14:57.327 --> 00:14:58.794
I'm scared.

00:14:58.829 --> 00:15:00.456
I believe you can help it.

00:15:00.497 --> 00:15:03.432
Vulcan children learn to detach
themselves from their emotions

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.865
at an early age.

00:15:04.901 --> 00:15:06.027
How?

00:15:06.069 --> 00:15:09.971
First, you must focus
on the object of your fear.

00:15:10.007 --> 00:15:13.534
Picture the morrok
clearly in your minds.

00:15:16.046 --> 00:15:20.039
That image is accompanied
by an emotional response.

00:15:20.083 --> 00:15:22.313
Describe for me
what that feeling is like.

00:15:22.352 --> 00:15:24.877
It makes my stomach all tight.

00:15:24.921 --> 00:15:28.015
I feel like I want to run,
but my legs won't work.

00:15:28.058 --> 00:15:30.458
Now, if you could see this
emotion in physical form,

00:15:30.527 --> 00:15:32.085
what would it look like?

00:15:32.129 --> 00:15:34.324
It's like this big black cloud

00:15:34.364 --> 00:15:37.390
with lots of thunder
and lightning all around us.

00:15:37.434 --> 00:15:40.597
Then imagine a strong wind
is pushing that cloud away.

00:15:40.637 --> 00:15:43.834
Watch as your fear
grows more distant.

00:15:43.874 --> 00:15:46.672
It is no longer a part of you.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.109
Once you begin

00:15:48.145 --> 00:15:51.080
to detach yourselves
from your emotional responses,

00:15:51.114 --> 00:15:53.275
you come closer
to controlling them.

00:15:53.316 --> 00:15:55.876
Eventually, they will be
eliminated altogether.

00:15:55.919 --> 00:15:58.581
Do you live your whole life
without feeling anything?

00:15:58.622 --> 00:16:02.217
More accurately, we strive
to control our feelings.

00:16:02.259 --> 00:16:04.523
You don't get scared... ever?

00:16:04.561 --> 00:16:05.789
No.

00:16:05.829 --> 00:16:07.854
Even when your shuttle crashed?

00:16:07.898 --> 00:16:09.024
That is correct.

00:16:09.066 --> 00:16:10.431
But what if there was

00:16:10.467 --> 00:16:12.332
this big hairy tardeth
coming after you...

00:16:12.369 --> 00:16:14.769
The circumstances
are irrelevant.

00:16:14.805 --> 00:16:17.330
A Vulcan approaches
every situation logically.

00:16:17.374 --> 00:16:20.002
Now, I must begin work
on my shuttle.

00:16:20.043 --> 00:16:22.204
We will resume the search
for the other children

00:16:22.245 --> 00:16:23.735
once the sensors
are operational.

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:26.340
I expect each of you
to sit quietly

00:16:26.383 --> 00:16:28.442
and not touch
any of the equipment.

00:16:28.552 --> 00:16:30.577
We promise.

00:16:33.156 --> 00:16:36.148
Elani, please, put that down.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.184
Let me have it!

00:16:38.228 --> 00:16:39.695
No! I found it!

00:16:41.298 --> 00:16:42.822
Be careful with that!

00:16:45.168 --> 00:16:46.260
You...

00:16:46.303 --> 00:16:48.168
will stay here.

00:16:49.973 --> 00:16:52.168
And you...

00:16:52.209 --> 00:16:54.177
will stay here.

00:16:54.211 --> 00:16:55.678
Where do I get to sit?

00:16:59.349 --> 00:17:01.715
But I want to sit next to you.

00:17:19.302 --> 00:17:20.667
Tuvok?

00:17:20.704 --> 00:17:21.671
Yes?

00:17:21.705 --> 00:17:23.900
Why do your ears
look like that?

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.408
All Vulcans have
similarly shaped ears.

00:17:26.443 --> 00:17:27.774
Why?

00:17:27.811 --> 00:17:30.336
It is a result
of many millennia of evolution.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.904
Do they make you hear better?

00:17:31.948 --> 00:17:33.882
No.

00:17:33.917 --> 00:17:35.248
Where do Vulcans live?

00:17:35.285 --> 00:17:36.650
Is it far away?

00:17:36.686 --> 00:17:40.679
My homeworld is on the
other side of the galaxy.

00:17:40.724 --> 00:17:42.316
Elani. Elani!

00:17:42.359 --> 00:17:44.554
I asked you not
to play with that.

00:17:44.594 --> 00:17:45.583
Sorry.

00:17:50.133 --> 00:17:51.930
What are you doing?

00:17:51.968 --> 00:17:54.994
It helps prepare you to
attain a meditative state.

00:17:55.038 --> 00:17:56.596
Now close your eyes

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.131
and imagine
all the energy in your body

00:17:59.176 --> 00:18:02.407
is flowing to the point
where your fingertips meet.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:07.316
Nothing else you hear
or feel is important.

00:18:08.952 --> 00:18:11.785
Let the outside world fade away.

00:18:11.822 --> 00:18:14.552
You exist only inside your mind.

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:18.222
Tuvok?

00:18:18.261 --> 00:18:19.353
Yes?

00:18:19.396 --> 00:18:21.125
Do you have any children?

00:18:21.164 --> 00:18:22.392
Be quiet.

00:18:22.432 --> 00:18:25.765
We are trying to attain
a meditative state.

00:18:25.802 --> 00:18:26.996
But I want to know.

00:18:27.037 --> 00:18:28.664
I have four children.

00:18:28.705 --> 00:18:30.468
Now, you must concentrate.

00:18:32.175 --> 00:18:33.665
What are they like?

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.701
Well-behaved.

00:18:35.745 --> 00:18:37.610
They had already mastered

00:18:37.647 --> 00:18:39.274
several states of
heightened awareness

00:18:39.316 --> 00:18:40.908
by the time they were your age.

00:18:40.951 --> 00:18:43.146
If Vulcans don't feel anything,

00:18:43.186 --> 00:18:44.881
does that mean
you don't love them?

00:18:46.656 --> 00:18:48.351
My attachment to my children

00:18:48.391 --> 00:18:50.416
cannot be described
as an emotion.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:53.395
They are part of my identity.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.762
And I am...

00:18:55.799 --> 00:18:58.461
incomplete without them.

00:18:58.501 --> 00:19:01.800
I bet they miss you, too.

00:19:02.839 --> 00:19:04.170
Tuvok?

00:19:04.207 --> 00:19:05.367
Yes?

00:19:05.408 --> 00:19:07.638
I have to scratch my nose.

00:19:07.677 --> 00:19:09.076
You may.

00:19:09.112 --> 00:19:11.410
Tuvok!

00:19:11.448 --> 00:19:12.608
Yes!

00:19:12.649 --> 00:19:14.276
I hear something.

00:19:14.317 --> 00:19:16.012
Is it a ship?

00:19:16.052 --> 00:19:17.451
I believe so.

00:19:22.726 --> 00:19:24.421
Can you see who it is?

00:19:24.494 --> 00:19:26.792
The sensors are
only partially functional.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.422
I'm attempting
to identify the ship

00:19:28.531 --> 00:19:30.123
by its shield harmonics.

00:19:30.166 --> 00:19:32.157
Is somebody coming to save us?

00:19:32.202 --> 00:19:34.329
It is not a shuttle
from Voyager.

00:19:34.371 --> 00:19:36.805
The pattern of the harmonics
matches that of the ships

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:39.001
we scanned in orbit
around Drayan.

00:19:39.042 --> 00:19:41.875
It seems your people
have come looking for you.

00:19:43.013 --> 00:19:45.038
We have to hide, Tuvok.

00:19:45.081 --> 00:19:46.776
You can't let them find us here.

00:19:46.816 --> 00:19:48.215
I don't understand.

00:19:48.251 --> 00:19:50.617
I thought you wanted to go home.

00:19:50.654 --> 00:19:52.053
They won't take us home.

00:19:52.088 --> 00:19:54.215
They're the ones
who made us come here.

00:19:54.257 --> 00:19:56.020
For what purpose?

00:19:56.059 --> 00:19:58.857
They sent us here to die.

00:20:05.601 --> 00:20:07.068
We have to go.

00:20:07.103 --> 00:20:09.003
If they find us, we'll all die.

00:20:09.038 --> 00:20:10.266
Please, Tuvok.

00:20:10.306 --> 00:20:12.866
Why would your own people
want to harm you?

00:20:12.909 --> 00:20:14.399
Please.
They're coming.

00:20:14.444 --> 00:20:16.207
Help us.

00:20:32.061 --> 00:20:33.585
Any indication
where they've gone?

00:20:33.629 --> 00:20:34.653
No.

00:20:34.697 --> 00:20:36.062
Spread out and scan the area.

00:20:39.168 --> 00:20:41.033
Two of them are coming this way.

00:20:42.238 --> 00:20:43.603
What are you doing?

00:20:43.639 --> 00:20:45.539
This will hide us
from their scanners.

00:21:08.865 --> 00:21:10.833
I'm not picking up
any life-forms this way.

00:21:29.852 --> 00:21:31.752
Why do you believe
they've come to kill you?

00:21:31.787 --> 00:21:33.220
We're supposed to die here.

00:21:33.256 --> 00:21:35.156
That's what this place is for.

00:21:35.191 --> 00:21:37.989
They bring children here
for the final ritual.

00:21:38.027 --> 00:21:40.393
Then the morrok takes them away.

00:21:40.429 --> 00:21:41.862
No one ever comes back.

00:21:41.898 --> 00:21:45.459
It is illogical for a society
to kill its own children.

00:21:45.501 --> 00:21:48.026
The scrolls say
we should be happy...

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:51.471
that when we die, the energy
inside us is set free.

00:21:51.507 --> 00:21:52.940
Is it true?

00:21:52.975 --> 00:21:55.000
Is that what really happens?

00:21:55.044 --> 00:21:58.844
Vulcans believe
that a person's katra...

00:21:58.881 --> 00:22:00.906
what some might call a soul...

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:03.851
continues to exist
after the body dies.

00:22:03.886 --> 00:22:05.478
Do you believe that?

00:22:06.489 --> 00:22:09.720
When I was younger,
I accepted it without question.

00:22:09.759 --> 00:22:13.320
In recent years, I have
experienced doubts.

00:22:13.362 --> 00:22:16.160
I do believe there is
more within each of us

00:22:16.198 --> 00:22:18.393
than science has yet explained.

00:22:18.434 --> 00:22:20.868
I know
we should have more faith.

00:22:20.903 --> 00:22:22.837
It's wrong
to be afraid of death.

00:22:22.872 --> 00:22:25.864
There is nothing wrong
in choosing to live.

00:22:25.908 --> 00:22:27.739
Will you help us?

00:22:27.777 --> 00:22:29.438
Until I can gain
a better understanding

00:22:29.478 --> 00:22:32.208
of your situation,
I believe it would be best

00:22:32.248 --> 00:22:34.443
to get you safely
back to Voyager.

00:22:42.124 --> 00:22:44.024
Torres and Neelix just got back,

00:22:44.060 --> 00:22:46.324
but there's still no word
from Tuvok and Bennet.

00:22:46.362 --> 00:22:49.160
I'm not picking up
their shuttle on sensors.

00:22:49.198 --> 00:22:50.631
There's heavy
solar flare activity.

00:22:50.666 --> 00:22:52.497
It's causing
electrodynamic disturbance

00:22:52.602 --> 00:22:53.762
throughout the system.

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:57.668
We found a vein
of pure polyferranide

00:22:57.707 --> 00:22:58.833
three kilometers long.

00:22:58.874 --> 00:22:59.863
It's a real shame we're leaving.

00:22:59.909 --> 00:23:01.877
When was your last contact
with the other team?

00:23:01.911 --> 00:23:04.004
Several hours ago.
Is there a problem?

00:23:04.046 --> 00:23:05.536
We can't reach them.

00:23:05.581 --> 00:23:06.639
When we spoke to them,

00:23:06.682 --> 00:23:08.650
they were going to check out
the outermost moons.

00:23:08.684 --> 00:23:11.448
Can you find
the shuttle's ion signature?

00:23:11.554 --> 00:23:15.012
I'm reading one
on heading 151 mark 8.

00:23:15.057 --> 00:23:17.685
That's where Neelix and I went.

00:23:17.727 --> 00:23:19.160
And another one
on a divergent course,

00:23:19.195 --> 00:23:20.856
20 degrees to starboard.

00:23:20.896 --> 00:23:23.160
Set a course, Mr. Paris.

00:23:30.206 --> 00:23:32.071
Our scans of the moon
are inconclusive.

00:23:32.108 --> 00:23:33.075
We can't see anything

00:23:33.109 --> 00:23:34.576
through the turbulence
in the atmosphere.

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:37.170
The Drayan ship still hasn't
responded to our hails.

00:23:37.213 --> 00:23:39.147
Are you sure our signal's
getting through?

00:23:39.181 --> 00:23:40.842
They're receiving it.

00:23:40.883 --> 00:23:42.145
They're just not answering.

00:23:42.184 --> 00:23:43.344
Continue hails.

00:23:43.386 --> 00:23:46.048
This desecration
dishonors us both, Captain.

00:23:46.088 --> 00:23:47.248
I'm sorry.
I don't understand...

00:23:47.289 --> 00:23:50.053
This moon is our crysata...
sacred ground.

00:23:50.092 --> 00:23:52.185
Your presence is forbidden here.

00:23:52.228 --> 00:23:54.492
We've only come here
to look for one of our shuttles.

00:23:54.597 --> 00:23:56.326
It's missing.

00:23:56.365 --> 00:23:58.060
We found your shuttle
on the surface.

00:23:58.100 --> 00:23:59.067
The pilot is dead.

00:23:59.101 --> 00:24:01.069
There were two men on board.

00:24:01.103 --> 00:24:02.627
Did you find both of them?

00:24:02.672 --> 00:24:03.969
No, only one.

00:24:04.006 --> 00:24:05.701
If there's someone else
on this moon,

00:24:05.741 --> 00:24:08.107
you must transport him back
to your ship immediately.

00:24:08.144 --> 00:24:09.805
That's what we intend to do.

00:24:09.845 --> 00:24:10.903
This kind of disturbance

00:24:10.946 --> 00:24:13.915
is exactly why we avoid contact
with outsiders.

00:24:13.949 --> 00:24:15.917
I was wrong to respond
to your communication.

00:24:15.951 --> 00:24:18.442
I should have known better
than to indulge my curiosity.

00:24:18.521 --> 00:24:19.749
There's no one at fault here.

00:24:19.789 --> 00:24:21.416
The shuttle crash
was an accident.

00:24:21.457 --> 00:24:24.449
One which I expect you
to correct as soon as possible.

00:24:26.696 --> 00:24:27.993
What's the status
of the transporters?

00:24:28.030 --> 00:24:29.122
The targeting scanners

00:24:29.165 --> 00:24:30.826
still can't lock on to anything
on the surface.

00:24:30.866 --> 00:24:33.027
It would be easier
if we sent down another shuttle.

00:24:33.069 --> 00:24:35.367
No, that would only
make things worse.

00:24:36.405 --> 00:24:37.736
I'll keep working on it.

00:24:52.588 --> 00:24:54.419
I don't see how you
could be thirsty again

00:24:54.457 --> 00:24:56.049
after four drinks of water.

00:24:56.092 --> 00:24:57.855
Aren't you going to sleep?

00:24:57.893 --> 00:25:00.453
I can go several days
without rest if necessary.

00:25:00.496 --> 00:25:02.657
You cannot.

00:25:02.698 --> 00:25:05.064
It's warmer by the fire.

00:25:05.101 --> 00:25:08.070
Go back and try to sleep.

00:25:08.104 --> 00:25:10.197
Do not worry.

00:25:10.239 --> 00:25:12.799
I have run several
thorough scans of the area.

00:25:12.842 --> 00:25:14.901
There are no other
life-forms present...

00:25:14.944 --> 00:25:15.911
inside the cave

00:25:15.945 --> 00:25:18.140
or anywhere
within five kilometers.

00:25:18.180 --> 00:25:21.445
Maybe the morrok doesn't
show up on the scans.

00:25:21.484 --> 00:25:24.044
I am also keeping watch
on all of you from here.

00:25:24.086 --> 00:25:25.576
If there is any
indication of trouble,

00:25:25.621 --> 00:25:27.384
I'll come immediately.

00:25:27.423 --> 00:25:28.685
Okay.

00:25:46.842 --> 00:25:48.810
We can't sleep.

00:25:50.746 --> 00:25:52.304
Apparently not.

00:25:52.348 --> 00:25:53.679
It's so dark.

00:25:53.716 --> 00:25:55.616
I think the fire's going out.

00:25:55.651 --> 00:25:57.778
Maybe you should look.

00:25:57.820 --> 00:26:00.482
I added more wood
less than a half an hour ago.

00:26:01.624 --> 00:26:05.025
However, it might be wise
to check it again.

00:26:06.896 --> 00:26:09.660
I always have my hair brushed
before I go to sleep.

00:26:09.698 --> 00:26:11.757
I like to hear a story.

00:26:11.801 --> 00:26:14.429
Tell us one
about the fire beast of Sullus.

00:26:14.470 --> 00:26:16.370
I never understood
the practice in some cultures

00:26:16.405 --> 00:26:18.396
of describing
ferocious creatures

00:26:18.440 --> 00:26:20.431
in an attempt
to lull children to sleep.

00:26:20.543 --> 00:26:22.738
Don't Vulcans tell
bedtime stories?

00:26:22.778 --> 00:26:25.747
If my children
had difficulty sleeping,

00:26:25.781 --> 00:26:27.442
I would play music for them.

00:26:27.516 --> 00:26:29.848
I like music.

00:26:29.885 --> 00:26:32.376
Unfortunately,
I don't have my lute.

00:26:32.421 --> 00:26:33.718
What's that?

00:26:33.756 --> 00:26:35.348
It is a five-stringed
instrument

00:26:35.391 --> 00:26:37.552
tuned on a diatonic scale.

00:26:37.593 --> 00:26:39.959
It can be very soothing.

00:26:39.995 --> 00:26:43.055
My youngest son was
particularly fond of it.

00:26:44.166 --> 00:26:48.262
He always used to ask me
to play "Falor's Journey."

00:26:48.304 --> 00:26:52.968
It is a tale of enlightenment
consisting of 348 verses.

00:26:57.479 --> 00:27:00.880
It may not be necessary to
include the complete narrative.

00:27:00.916 --> 00:27:03.214
Falor was a prosperous merchant

00:27:03.252 --> 00:27:06.244
who went on a journey
to gain greater awareness.

00:27:06.288 --> 00:27:10.657
"Through storms,
he crossed the Voroth Sea

00:27:10.693 --> 00:27:15.130
"to reach the clouded
shores of Raal,

00:27:15.164 --> 00:27:17.564
where old T'Para offered truth."

00:27:18.968 --> 00:27:23.564
He traveled
through the windswept hills

00:27:23.606 --> 00:27:28.407
And crossed
the barren Fire Plains

00:27:28.444 --> 00:27:34.280
To find the silent monks
of Kir

00:27:34.316 --> 00:27:37.080
Still unfulfilled

00:27:37.119 --> 00:27:39.679
He journeyed home

00:27:39.722 --> 00:27:45.126
Told stories
of the lessons learned

00:27:45.160 --> 00:27:53.761
And gained true wisdom
by the giving...

00:28:26.702 --> 00:28:29.398
Tuvok! Tuvok!

00:28:31.707 --> 00:28:32.901
They're gone.

00:28:46.820 --> 00:28:48.651
Captain, you might want
to see this.

00:28:48.689 --> 00:28:50.156
Have you found the shuttle?

00:28:50.190 --> 00:28:52.317
Actually, we've found two.

00:28:52.359 --> 00:28:53.917
Both crashed on the surface.

00:28:53.961 --> 00:28:56.361
The sensor resolution
is still quite low.

00:28:56.396 --> 00:28:57.863
This looks like our shuttle.

00:28:57.898 --> 00:29:00.196
I'd guess the other one
is Drayan.

00:29:00.234 --> 00:29:02.930
We've also had some indications
of life signs on the surface.

00:29:02.970 --> 00:29:05.097
A while ago, there seemed
to be four of them.

00:29:05.139 --> 00:29:07.630
Now we can only distinguish two.

00:29:07.674 --> 00:29:10.268
I've been working
on the transporters.

00:29:10.310 --> 00:29:12.801
It just isn't possible
to get a pattern lock

00:29:12.846 --> 00:29:13.972
through all the turbulence.

00:29:14.014 --> 00:29:16.505
Then we've got to start
considering other options.

00:29:16.550 --> 00:29:19.110
I want a full analysis
of the atmospheric conditions

00:29:19.153 --> 00:29:21.986
and your best suggestion of how
to get a shuttle to the surface.

00:29:22.022 --> 00:29:24.047
Then let's hope
we won't need to try it.

00:29:28.228 --> 00:29:29.991
There were no other life-forms

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:33.022
and no unusual energy readings
within sensor range all night.

00:29:33.066 --> 00:29:34.226
It was the morrok.

00:29:34.268 --> 00:29:36.031
Why don't you believe me?

00:29:36.069 --> 00:29:38.902
Very well.

00:29:38.939 --> 00:29:40.907
I'll investigate.

00:29:40.941 --> 00:29:44.206
I'd like you to wait here
while I look inside the cave.

00:29:44.244 --> 00:29:47.771
But if you go in there,
you won't come out.

00:29:47.814 --> 00:29:50.078
I will take
every possible precaution.

00:29:53.153 --> 00:29:56.316
I believe you can be responsible
with this.

00:29:56.356 --> 00:29:58.381
Aim like this

00:29:58.425 --> 00:30:00.416
and press here to fire.

00:30:00.460 --> 00:30:02.985
I'll seal the shuttle's
door while I'm gone.

00:30:03.030 --> 00:30:07.126
No, Tuvok. Don't leave me
all by myself. Please!

00:30:07.167 --> 00:30:08.964
If there is anything
in the cave,

00:30:09.002 --> 00:30:11.903
it may help us determine
what has been happening here.

00:30:11.939 --> 00:30:15.807
It is very important to gather
as much information as possible.

00:30:15.842 --> 00:30:17.901
I'm scared.

00:30:17.945 --> 00:30:21.437
We often fear
what we do not understand.

00:30:21.481 --> 00:30:24.041
Our best defense is knowledge.

00:30:24.084 --> 00:30:25.915
You must trust me, Tressa.

00:30:25.953 --> 00:30:27.477
I'll return shortly.

00:30:27.521 --> 00:30:29.216
Promise?

00:30:29.256 --> 00:30:31.053
I will not abandon you.

00:32:23.103 --> 00:32:25.401
What did you see in there?

00:32:25.439 --> 00:32:30.843
I realize it may frighten you,
but you must hear the truth.

00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:36.274
Suffice it to say, I did not
find the other children,

00:32:36.316 --> 00:32:40.047
nor do I have any explanation
of what happened to them.

00:32:40.087 --> 00:32:42.487
I'm going to be next, aren't I?

00:32:42.589 --> 00:32:43.988
There's nothing
we can do about it.

00:32:44.024 --> 00:32:47.619
The disappearances have
occurred only at night.

00:32:47.661 --> 00:32:50.755
We will attempt to leave
here before the sun sets.

00:32:50.797 --> 00:32:53.027
I'll really be quiet this time.

00:32:53.066 --> 00:32:54.499
I won't touch anything.

00:32:54.601 --> 00:32:56.796
That would make it
difficult for you

00:32:56.837 --> 00:32:58.498
to assist me with repairs.

00:33:00.240 --> 00:33:01.935
The Drayans have just
sent another shuttle

00:33:01.975 --> 00:33:03.033
down to the moon, Captain.

00:33:03.076 --> 00:33:06.102
There must be at least 20
people on the surface.

00:33:06.146 --> 00:33:07.670
I can't tell
if the two life-forms

00:33:07.714 --> 00:33:09.306
we detected before
are still there.

00:33:09.349 --> 00:33:11.283
How many search parties
could it take

00:33:11.318 --> 00:33:12.717
to find two crash victims?

00:33:12.753 --> 00:33:14.220
Captain, there's a break
in the turbulence.

00:33:14.254 --> 00:33:15.653
I'm picking up a com signal.

00:33:15.689 --> 00:33:18.624
Tuvok to Voyager.
Voyager, do you read?

00:33:18.658 --> 00:33:20.558
We read you, Tuvok.
Are you all right?

00:33:20.594 --> 00:33:23.062
Yes, Captain,
but Ensign Bennet is dead.

00:33:23.096 --> 00:33:24.063
We know.

00:33:24.097 --> 00:33:25.689
We've been trying to get you
off the surface,

00:33:25.732 --> 00:33:27.427
but we're having some trouble
with the Drayans.

00:33:27.467 --> 00:33:29.332
They insist on sending
their own search parties.

00:33:29.369 --> 00:33:31.701
Yes, I have been avoiding them.

00:33:31.738 --> 00:33:32.705
Why?

00:33:32.739 --> 00:33:33.831
I have a young girl with me

00:33:33.874 --> 00:33:35.774
who claims
they have come to kill her.

00:33:35.809 --> 00:33:37.936
I was reluctant
to believe it at first,

00:33:37.978 --> 00:33:40.606
but several other children
have disappeared.

00:33:43.016 --> 00:33:44.381
There's nothing I can do,
Captain.

00:33:44.418 --> 00:33:45.407
The signal's breaking up.

00:33:45.452 --> 00:33:48.080
Tuvok, what happened
to the other children?

00:33:48.121 --> 00:33:49.486
They have disappeared.

00:33:49.589 --> 00:33:52.057
Something on this moon
is responsible.

00:33:52.092 --> 00:33:53.286
We must leave here.

00:33:53.326 --> 00:33:55.021
I'm attempting to repair...

00:33:56.797 --> 00:33:58.230
Scan Tuvok's shuttle for damage.

00:33:58.265 --> 00:34:00.256
Will he be able to get himself
out of there?

00:34:00.300 --> 00:34:01.597
There's no structural damage.

00:34:01.635 --> 00:34:03.262
Some power fluctuations.

00:34:03.303 --> 00:34:05.168
He should be able to take off.

00:34:05.205 --> 00:34:06.604
What if they can't?

00:34:07.941 --> 00:34:09.738
Hail the Drayan ship.

00:34:09.776 --> 00:34:12.404
Captain.

00:34:12.446 --> 00:34:15.074
First Prelate,
it's come to my attention

00:34:15.115 --> 00:34:17.208
that you have a damaged ship
on the surface as well

00:34:17.250 --> 00:34:18.945
and there may be survivors.

00:34:18.985 --> 00:34:21.112
I'd like to offer our help
in finding them.

00:34:21.154 --> 00:34:22.348
Perhaps a joint
rescue operation...

00:34:22.389 --> 00:34:24.357
That won't be necessary,
Captain.

00:34:24.391 --> 00:34:25.790
You've been intrusive enough.

00:34:25.826 --> 00:34:27.384
Our sensor readings indicate

00:34:27.427 --> 00:34:29.327
the people on the surface
may be in trouble.

00:34:29.362 --> 00:34:30.454
I'm sure you must be

00:34:30.530 --> 00:34:32.794
as concerned
for their safety as we are.

00:34:32.833 --> 00:34:35.825
There's no reason to fear for
anyone's safety on the crysata.

00:34:35.869 --> 00:34:38.463
It's a blessed haven,
sheltered and unspoiled,

00:34:38.538 --> 00:34:40.563
which is the very reason
why I can't allow you

00:34:40.607 --> 00:34:43.041
to go there
under any circumstances.

00:34:43.076 --> 00:34:45.738
Then I regret to inform you
I'll be taking a shuttle

00:34:45.779 --> 00:34:48.111
to the surface
without your permission.

00:34:48.148 --> 00:34:49.479
That's completely unacceptable.

00:34:49.549 --> 00:34:51.244
I believe it's necessary.

00:34:51.284 --> 00:34:53.252
If you launch
one of your shuttles,

00:34:53.286 --> 00:34:55.117
I will be forced to send
one of ours after you.

00:34:55.155 --> 00:34:58.591
First Prelate, it's not my
intention to provoke a conflict.

00:34:58.625 --> 00:34:59.887
Well, then leave at once.

00:34:59.926 --> 00:35:02.190
I'll be glad to, as soon
as every member of my crew

00:35:02.229 --> 00:35:04.288
is safely back on board
this ship.

00:35:04.331 --> 00:35:05.821
Janeway out.

00:35:06.867 --> 00:35:07.993
Lieutenant, you're with me.

00:35:09.302 --> 00:35:11.167
Mr. Kim, I need your report.

00:35:11.204 --> 00:35:13.104
I've been studying
the energy signature

00:35:13.139 --> 00:35:14.299
of the Drayan shuttles.

00:35:14.341 --> 00:35:16.366
They're using some kind
of dielectric field

00:35:16.409 --> 00:35:18.104
to protect them
from the turbulence.

00:35:18.144 --> 00:35:19.736
We could generate
the same kind of field

00:35:19.779 --> 00:35:21.212
with our shuttle's warp coils.

00:35:21.248 --> 00:35:22.613
It won't be very stable.

00:35:22.649 --> 00:35:24.879
It might be a rough ride,
but we can make it.

00:35:24.918 --> 00:35:26.852
Captain, maybe you shouldn't...

00:35:26.887 --> 00:35:28.787
I know the risks, Commander,
but if there's any hope

00:35:28.822 --> 00:35:30.722
left for a diplomatic solution,

00:35:30.757 --> 00:35:32.657
I've got to be down there
to see it through.

00:35:43.336 --> 00:35:45.861
Let's get through
the preflight quickly.

00:35:45.906 --> 00:35:50.138
Thrusters, impulse
engines, warp drive...

00:35:50.176 --> 00:35:52.440
All propulsion systems
are nominal.

00:35:52.479 --> 00:35:56.813
Shields, phasers, inertial
dampers, com system.

00:35:56.850 --> 00:35:58.112
I think we've got
all the basics.

00:35:58.151 --> 00:36:00.881
Computer, initiate
cold launch sequence.

00:36:00.921 --> 00:36:03.651
Or we could just skip
preflight altogether.

00:36:03.690 --> 00:36:05.920
Definitely not recommended,
but sometimes necessary.

00:36:05.959 --> 00:36:06.948
I'll remember that.

00:36:06.993 --> 00:36:10.019
I'm taking the warp drive
off-line.

00:36:10.063 --> 00:36:12.429
Setting up the dielectric field.

00:36:12.532 --> 00:36:14.727
It's holding, but we'll
have to keep an eye

00:36:14.768 --> 00:36:16.565
on the stabilizer integrity.

00:36:16.603 --> 00:36:17.695
Janeway to Bridge.

00:36:17.737 --> 00:36:20.205
Depressurize the shuttle bay
and open the space doors.

00:36:20.240 --> 00:36:21.434
Aye, Captain.

00:36:28.715 --> 00:36:30.273
Captain, I'm picking up
a Drayan shuttle.

00:36:30.317 --> 00:36:32.148
They're on an intercept course.

00:36:32.185 --> 00:36:33.174
Can we outrun them?

00:36:37.791 --> 00:36:38.883
The dielectric field

00:36:38.925 --> 00:36:40.984
is weakening our
structural integrity.

00:36:41.027 --> 00:36:43.120
If we go much faster,
I'm afraid we'll break up.

00:36:43.163 --> 00:36:44.892
We're improvising here.

00:36:44.931 --> 00:36:45.989
The Drayans aren't.

00:36:46.032 --> 00:36:47.590
We're on their home turf.

00:36:47.634 --> 00:36:48.999
They have every advantage.

00:36:49.035 --> 00:36:51.799
That may be reason enough
for them not to fire on us.

00:36:51.838 --> 00:36:54.705
We'll be testing that theory
in a few seconds.

00:36:54.741 --> 00:36:56.834
They're about to enter
weapons range, Captain.

00:36:56.876 --> 00:36:58.002
Raise shields to maximum

00:36:58.044 --> 00:37:00.808
and stand ready
to power the weapons.

00:37:07.218 --> 00:37:08.310
Maneuvering thrusters

00:37:08.353 --> 00:37:10.218
and impulse engines
are functional.

00:37:10.255 --> 00:37:11.950
We're ready to lift off.

00:37:11.990 --> 00:37:13.890
What about the electro?

00:37:13.925 --> 00:37:16.189
The currents
that made the ships crash?

00:37:16.227 --> 00:37:17.888
I have determined
that a dielectric field

00:37:17.929 --> 00:37:19.726
should allow us
to pass through them.

00:37:19.764 --> 00:37:22.392
However, you should still be
prepared for some turbulence.

00:37:23.602 --> 00:37:25.570
Initiating prelaunch sequence.

00:37:26.605 --> 00:37:28.163
Number three thruster
is failing.

00:37:28.206 --> 00:37:29.400
Attempting to stabilize.

00:37:33.445 --> 00:37:35.811
Drayan shuttle's closing fast,
Captain.

00:37:35.847 --> 00:37:37.610
They'll overtake us
before we can land.

00:37:37.649 --> 00:37:39.640
They haven't powered
their weapon systems.

00:37:39.684 --> 00:37:41.208
Maybe they're
still willing to talk.

00:37:41.252 --> 00:37:44.221
Let's hope the ones on the
surface feel the same way.

00:37:45.690 --> 00:37:48.181
We'll be through this ionosphere
in a few more minutes.

00:37:48.226 --> 00:37:49.716
Sensors are clearing up.

00:37:49.761 --> 00:37:52.229
I'm reading Tuvok's shuttle.

00:37:52.263 --> 00:37:54.197
He's trying to lift off,
but it looks

00:37:54.232 --> 00:37:55.790
like there's some trouble
with the thrusters.

00:37:56.968 --> 00:37:58.697
And there's
a large Drayan search party

00:37:58.737 --> 00:38:00.466
approaching his location.

00:38:02.007 --> 00:38:03.497
I see them.

00:38:03.541 --> 00:38:05.406
They're coming all around us.

00:38:05.477 --> 00:38:07.308
We've got to go... now.

00:38:07.345 --> 00:38:08.778
I'm attempting
an emergency procedure.

00:38:08.813 --> 00:38:10.474
Please move away
from the console.

00:38:26.231 --> 00:38:27.892
You did it!

00:38:27.932 --> 00:38:29.661
You saved me.

00:38:29.701 --> 00:38:31.931
I regret that may be
a premature conclusion.

00:38:31.970 --> 00:38:33.665
The process
of powering the thrusters

00:38:33.705 --> 00:38:36.435
has left us with minimal shields
and no functional weapons.

00:38:36.541 --> 00:38:38.941
Voyager will be
watching for us.

00:38:38.977 --> 00:38:40.137
When we clear the atmosphere,

00:38:40.178 --> 00:38:41.702
we can be transported
aboard the ship.

00:38:41.746 --> 00:38:43.441
Then what are we going to do?

00:38:43.481 --> 00:38:45.813
You may request asylum
with the Federation if you wish.

00:38:45.850 --> 00:38:47.784
Then we'll be able
to protect you.

00:38:47.819 --> 00:38:49.684
I want to stay with you.

00:38:51.089 --> 00:38:53.182
The Drayan shuttle
is hailing us.

00:38:53.224 --> 00:38:55.021
You're holding
one of our children.

00:38:55.060 --> 00:38:56.357
I want to speak to her.

00:38:56.394 --> 00:38:58.294
She believes
you intend to kill her.

00:38:58.329 --> 00:38:59.455
Is that true?

00:38:59.564 --> 00:39:01.293
The child is confused.

00:39:01.332 --> 00:39:02.993
I only want to help her.

00:39:03.034 --> 00:39:04.729
You want me to die.

00:39:04.769 --> 00:39:08.034
Tressa, I understand how
confusing this must be for you.

00:39:08.073 --> 00:39:09.165
If you return to the surface,

00:39:09.207 --> 00:39:10.606
I will answer
all of your questions.

00:39:10.642 --> 00:39:12.974
No. I'm not going back there.

00:39:13.011 --> 00:39:15.241
I'm staying with Tuvok.

00:39:15.280 --> 00:39:17.805
We can resolve this matter
aboard Voyager.

00:39:17.849 --> 00:39:19.214
Unacceptable.

00:39:19.250 --> 00:39:20.308
If you or any of your people

00:39:20.351 --> 00:39:21.909
attempt to take Tressa
back to your ship,

00:39:21.953 --> 00:39:24.353
I will use any means necessary
to stop you.

00:39:24.389 --> 00:39:25.981
Do what you will.

00:39:27.225 --> 00:39:29.625
Very well.

00:39:29.661 --> 00:39:30.958
Fire.

00:39:36.701 --> 00:39:37.998
We weren't hit.

00:39:38.036 --> 00:39:39.867
I believe that was a warning.

00:39:42.240 --> 00:39:44.606
I've got phasers locked on
the Drayan shuttle, Captain.

00:39:44.642 --> 00:39:45.666
Don't fire.

00:39:45.710 --> 00:39:48.008
We might be able
to transport Tuvok from here.

00:39:49.214 --> 00:39:51.182
There's still
too much interference.

00:39:51.216 --> 00:39:54.117
We should be close enough
to get a com-signal through.

00:39:54.152 --> 00:39:56.620
Tuvok, we're on our way
to the surface.

00:39:56.654 --> 00:39:58.212
We'll intercept you
in a few moments.

00:39:58.256 --> 00:39:59.723
That may be too late, Captain.

00:39:59.758 --> 00:40:01.487
I'm losing power rapidly.

00:40:02.961 --> 00:40:05.259
I believe another hit
will force me to land.

00:40:05.296 --> 00:40:06.422
Go back down to the surface.

00:40:06.464 --> 00:40:07.453
We'll follow you.

00:40:12.570 --> 00:40:14.128
It's getting dark.

00:40:14.172 --> 00:40:15.867
What's going to happen to me?

00:40:15.907 --> 00:40:18.842
All I can tell you is,
I will be here with you.

00:40:23.882 --> 00:40:25.850
Mr. Tuvok, don't
make this difficult.

00:40:25.884 --> 00:40:27.909
She's been frightened enough.

00:40:27.952 --> 00:40:29.044
What she fears most

00:40:29.087 --> 00:40:31.078
is being kept here
against her wishes.

00:40:31.122 --> 00:40:32.589
This is a critical time.

00:40:32.624 --> 00:40:34.592
I can't allow you to interfere.

00:40:39.130 --> 00:40:40.791
I regret it's come to this.

00:40:40.832 --> 00:40:43.027
You have found your crew member.

00:40:43.067 --> 00:40:44.034
Now go.

00:40:44.068 --> 00:40:45.592
I will not leave without Tressa.

00:40:45.637 --> 00:40:48.504
She has asked for my protection,
and I intend to provide it.

00:40:48.540 --> 00:40:51.737
You simply don't understand
the harm you're doing.

00:40:51.776 --> 00:40:53.038
This child wants to live.

00:40:53.077 --> 00:40:55.637
We're going to do
whatever we can to help her.

00:40:55.680 --> 00:40:57.170
It is not a choice.

00:40:57.215 --> 00:40:59.274
This is her time.

00:40:59.317 --> 00:41:01.376
Tressa has reached
the end of her life.

00:41:01.419 --> 00:41:02.852
She has barely begun it.

00:41:02.887 --> 00:41:05.651
She is 96 years old.

00:41:08.359 --> 00:41:10.793
Tressa, these people
are outsiders.

00:41:10.829 --> 00:41:13.389
They don't understand
how we live.

00:41:13.431 --> 00:41:16.628
They see us as strange because
their aging process is reversed.

00:41:16.668 --> 00:41:19.000
Please, you don't belong
with them.

00:41:19.037 --> 00:41:20.766
I'm here to help you now.

00:41:20.805 --> 00:41:23.035
No. Leave me alone.

00:41:23.074 --> 00:41:26.043
It's perfectly natural
to be frightened.

00:41:26.077 --> 00:41:28.477
You're taking a step
into the unknown.

00:41:28.546 --> 00:41:30.810
The attendants would have
helped you prepare yourself.

00:41:30.849 --> 00:41:32.749
You were never meant to face
this time alone.

00:41:32.784 --> 00:41:34.342
We weren't alone.

00:41:34.385 --> 00:41:35.784
Tuvok was here.

00:41:35.820 --> 00:41:38.448
He stayed with us
and made us feel safe.

00:41:38.489 --> 00:41:40.719
He told us there was no morrok

00:41:40.758 --> 00:41:42.350
and that we shouldn't be afraid.

00:41:42.393 --> 00:41:44.361
He took care of us...

00:41:44.395 --> 00:41:49.332
even when we didn't behave
as well as Vulcan children.

00:41:49.367 --> 00:41:51.028
He was right about the morrok.

00:41:51.069 --> 00:41:54.038
It only exists in stories.

00:41:54.072 --> 00:41:57.303
At this age,
they become easily confused.

00:41:57.342 --> 00:41:58.866
Their memories are clouded.

00:41:58.910 --> 00:42:02.744
Near the end of life, we reach
a stage of complete innocence.

00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:05.943
We free ourselves from all
responsibilities to this life,

00:42:05.984 --> 00:42:07.576
then we leave it peacefully.

00:42:07.619 --> 00:42:09.450
Tressa doesn't seem to be ready.

00:42:09.554 --> 00:42:11.385
Perhaps she needs more time.

00:42:11.422 --> 00:42:13.947
That's not for you or me
to decide.

00:42:13.992 --> 00:42:16.085
This is
a normal biological process,

00:42:16.127 --> 00:42:18.220
which begins
the day we are created.

00:42:18.263 --> 00:42:20.561
The energy contained
within our bodies

00:42:20.598 --> 00:42:23.032
remains cohesive
for a limited number of years,

00:42:23.067 --> 00:42:24.364
and then it is released.

00:42:24.402 --> 00:42:26.461
Nothing can change that.

00:42:26.504 --> 00:42:28.267
Nothing?

00:42:28.306 --> 00:42:29.671
No.

00:42:29.707 --> 00:42:32.141
It's the natural course of life.

00:42:32.176 --> 00:42:33.973
Why was it so important
that Tressa stay here?

00:42:34.012 --> 00:42:35.309
We believe

00:42:35.346 --> 00:42:38.281
this is where the very first
spark of life was created.

00:42:38.316 --> 00:42:39.408
We are all compelled

00:42:39.450 --> 00:42:42.613
by a powerful instinct
to return here at the end,

00:42:42.654 --> 00:42:46.112
to complete the cycle
and rejoin the infinite energy.

00:42:46.157 --> 00:42:47.624
Tressa?

00:42:47.659 --> 00:42:49.126
Do you feel it calling to you?

00:42:49.160 --> 00:42:50.787
Tuvok?

00:42:53.665 --> 00:42:56.133
She can offer you
better guidance than I.

00:42:56.167 --> 00:42:58.158
You said you would protect me.

00:42:58.202 --> 00:42:59.226
I cannot protect you

00:42:59.270 --> 00:43:01.431
from the natural
conclusion of life,

00:43:01.472 --> 00:43:03.872
nor would I try.

00:43:03.908 --> 00:43:06.035
Vulcans consider death

00:43:06.077 --> 00:43:08.671
to be the completion
of a journey.

00:43:08.713 --> 00:43:11.147
There is nothing to fear.

00:43:11.182 --> 00:43:15.448
I won't be afraid,
not if you're with me.

00:43:16.921 --> 00:43:22.826
Tressa, may this night
see you safely home.

00:43:22.860 --> 00:43:27.297
Attending a child on the crysata
is an honorable role.

00:43:27.332 --> 00:43:29.698
You have fulfilled it well.

00:43:32.236 --> 00:43:35.228
The final moment of life
is the most sacred,

00:43:35.273 --> 00:43:36.831
most private time.

00:43:38.343 --> 00:43:41.005
I hope you can accept
my sincere apologies

00:43:41.045 --> 00:43:43.013
for disturbing your traditions.

00:43:44.215 --> 00:43:46.706
Perhaps we've each misjudged
the other, Captain.

00:43:46.751 --> 00:43:48.184
I would hate to let that ruin

00:43:48.219 --> 00:43:50.653
any possibility of friendship
between our people.

00:43:53.691 --> 00:43:55.181
We must leave them.

00:43:58.363 --> 00:44:01.730
Tuvok, can your shuttle
make it back to Voyager?

00:44:01.766 --> 00:44:03.757
Maybe we should wait for you.

00:44:03.801 --> 00:44:04.995
No, I'll be fine.

00:44:12.777 --> 00:44:15.177
We'll wait here
as long as you like.

00:44:15.213 --> 00:44:17.443
I know it's time.

00:44:17.548 --> 00:44:21.917
My only regret is leaving
my family, my grandson.

00:44:21.953 --> 00:44:23.978
You remind me of him sometimes.

00:44:26.891 --> 00:44:30.884
You will still be with them,
in their thoughts,

00:44:30.928 --> 00:44:34.864
as you will be in mine.
